window.DH=window.DH||{};window.DH["e04"]={"id":"e04","title":"第四集","parts":[{"id":"p01","title":"前情回顾，介绍 Lynette 的身份转变","lines":[{"id":"e04p0101","s":"Alice","t":"Previously on Desperate Housewives:","r":true,"m":["previously on（电视剧等）上集回顾 previously 以前地，先前地"]},{"id":"e04p0102","s":"Alice","t":"Susan played with fire and could get burned; Gabrielle found herself a playmate; Lynette couldn't get her kids to stop playing; and Bree played hardball. Everyone has a little dirty laundry.","r":true,"m":["play with fire 玩火：冒险尝试危险的事情，可能导致严重后果。","playmate n. 玩伴；游伴","get sb to do sth 使某人做某事，劝说某人做某事","play hardball 打硬球 = 强硬手段、不留情面","dirty laundry 家丑、不可告人的私事（不可数） laundry n.待洗的衣物；洗衣房，洗衣店；洗衣物，洗衣物的活"]},{"id":"e04p0103","s":"Alice","t":"When I was alive I maintained many different identities, lover, wife and ultimately victim.","r":true,"m":["maintained identities 持续投入力气去维护不同的身份 maintain v. 维持，保持 identity n. 身份，本体","ultimately adv. 最终，最后；根本上，最重要地","victim n. 受害者，罹难者；无助者，患病者；牺牲品，祭品；受骗者"]},{"id":"e04p0104","s":"Alice","t":"Yes, labels are important to the living, they dictate how people see themselves.","r":true,"m":["dictate v. 影响，支配；命令，规定；口述，使听写 n. 命令，规定","affect有影响 < influence改变倾向 < shape塑造 < dictate完全支配 + sb"]},{"id":"e04p0105","s":"Alice","t":"Like my friend Lynette, she used to see herself as a career woman, and a hugely successful one at that.","r":true,"m":["career woman 职业女性","hugely successful 固定搭配：非常成功的","and + 补充成分 + at that 而且……（还是相当……的那种）结构公式：X, and [更精确/更夸张的 X] at that."]},{"id":"e04p0106","s":"Alice","t":"She was known for her power lunches, her eye-catching presentations, and her ruthlessness in wiping out the competition.","r":true,"m":["power lunch 固定搭配：工作午餐，商务午餐","eye-catching adj.引人注目的；耀眼的；显著的","presentation n. 展示，展示；仪式，典礼；授予，颁发；赠予物；发布会","ruthlessness n.无情；冷酷；残忍","名词 + in + doing 在做某事方面的（某种品质）——介词 in 引出具体的行动领域","wipe out 彻底消灭、清除、彻底摧毁 wipe v.擦干净，抹掉 n.抹布，纸巾；擦拭","competition n. 竞争者，对手；竞争；比赛，竞赛 the competition 竞争对手（集合名词）"]},{"id":"e04p0107","s":"Alice","t":"But Lynette gave up her career to assume a new label, the incredibly satisfying role of full-time mother.","r":true,"m":["assume v. 承担、呈现、取得（身份/角色/权力）","incredibly adv.难以置信地；非常地","satisfying adj. 令人满意的；令人满足的 satisfied 感到满足的","full-time 全职 part-time兼职的 full-time mother / stay-at-home mom / housewife"]},{"id":"e04p0108","s":"Lynette","t":"Scavo residence. Yes, this is me.","r":true,"m":["residence n.住宅，住所；居住 Scavo residence. Scavo 府上，正式/老派的电话应答用语"]}]},{"id":"p02","title":"Lynette 因孩子闯祸接到老师谈话","lines":[{"id":"e04p0201","s":"Alice","t":"But unfortunately for Lynette, this new label frequently fell short of what was advertised.","r":true,"m":["frequently adv. 经常地，频繁地","fall short of 未达到，不足，不够：指某事物没有达到预期的程度或数量。","advertise v. 宣扬；为……做广告，登广告；公布，征聘；使变得显眼；"]},{"id":"e04p0202","s":"Lynette","t":"How in the world did they ...?","r":true,"m":["how in the world 究竟如何；到底怎么样：强烈的疑问某事是如何发生的"]},{"id":"e04p0203","s":"Teacher","t":"I left the door to the art supply cupboard open for five minutes, that's all, five minutes.","r":true,"m":["leave the door open 保持门开着","art supply 艺术用品 supply n. 供给量，储备；供应量；供应，补给 v. 供应，提供，供给；补充","cupboard n.橱柜。记忆：closet 是关起来的小屋（人也能进去），cupboard 是放杯子的架子（只伸手不伸人）"]},{"id":"e04p0204","s":"Lynette","t":"The little girl, why didn't she say anything?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0205","s":"Teacher","t":"Your boys work quickly.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0206","s":"Lynette","t":"Well, obviously, they will be punished for this, severely.","r":true,"m":["punish v. 处罚，惩罚；惩处；be punished for 因……而受到惩罚","severely adv. 非常严重地；严厉地，严肃地；朴素地 固定搭配：be punished severely受到严惩"]},{"id":"e04p0207","s":"Teacher","t":"I hesitate in bringing this up, since you got so ugly about it last time.","r":true,"m":["hesitate in doing sth 在做某事上犹豫不决== hesitate to do sth 搭配更常见","bring this up 提出这个问题或话题 bring up 提及，介绍","since 连词引导原因状语从句，既然；因为","you got so ugly about it 口语化, 你对此事的态度变得如此恶劣"]},{"id":"e04p0208","s":"Lynette","t":"They don't have attention deficit disorder, and I'm not gonna drug my boys just to make your job easier, I'd rather change teachers.","r":true,"m":["attention deficit disorder 注意力缺陷障碍 ADD","attention n. 注意；注意力；照料；兴趣；立正；殷勤，关心","deficit n. 亏损，赤字，不足额；（体育用语）失分数；缺乏，缺陷","disorder n. 混乱，杂乱；骚乱，动乱；紊乱，疾病 v. 打乱，使紊乱","drug 给……用药/下药","would rather do 宁愿做某事"]},{"id":"e04p0209","s":"Teacher","t":"The boys are in my class, because I'm the only teacher who can handle them.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0210","s":"Lynette","t":"What if we separate the twins, put them in different classes? They're much calmer when they're not bouncing off one another.","r":true,"m":["what if 如果…… 将会怎样；要是…… 怎么样","separate v. 分离；分成不同部分；隔开，阻隔 adj. 单独的，分开的；不同的","bounce off one another 固定口语搭配，专门形容小孩 / 一群人互相疯闹、追逐冲撞、精力互相传染，越闹越兴奋","one another == each other 都用于表达相互关系"]},{"id":"e04p0211","s":"Teacher","t":"We can try that. But if it doesn't work, we may no longer be able to accommodate them.","r":true,"m":["accommodate v. 接纳；为…提供住宿；容纳，提供空间；考虑到，顾及；顺应"]},{"id":"e04p0212","s":"Alice","t":"It suddenly occurred to Lynette, her label was about to change yet again.","r":true,"m":["occur to sb. 突然想到某个想法或主意，出现在某人的脑海中","yet again 再次，又一次。带情绪，不耐烦、无奈"]},{"id":"e04p0213","s":"Alice","t":"And for the next few years, she would be known as the mother of the boys who painted Tiffany Axelrod blue.","r":true,"m":["the next few years 随后几年，接下来几年","be known as被称为……/以……身份出名 be known for因……而出名","Tiffany Axelrod 小女孩的名字：蒂芙尼阿克塞尔罗德"]}]},{"id":"p03","title":"主妇们听 Mary Alice 的录音带","lines":[{"id":"e04p0301","s":"Alice","t":"It looked to be an interesting afternoon on Wisteria Lane, a mysterious cassette tape had been discovered by my friend Bree.","r":true,"m":["look to be 看起来像是 == look like","cassette tape 卡带，盒式磁带 cassette 磁带盒","tape 胶带，磁带，录音带 on the tape 在录音带上"]},{"id":"e04p0302","s":"Alice","t":"She had stolen it from her marriage counselor, a counselor I'd once spoken to in strictest confidence.","r":true,"m":["steal -- stole -- stolen v. 偷窃，盗窃；剽窃，窃取","in confidence 秘密地，不公开地(我告诉了你，但你得保密) confidence n. 自信；信任；把握；保密；秘密","strict adj. 要求严格的，严厉的 in strictest confidence 严格保密"]},{"id":"e04p0303","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"So how have you been?","r":true,"m":["How have you been? 你最近怎样？"]},{"id":"e04p0304","s":"Alice","t":"I had the nightmare again.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0305","s":"Gabrielle","t":"It's weird to hear Mary Alice.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0306","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Still the same one?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0307","s":"Alice","t":"Yes, but this time I was standing in a river and I saw the girl under the water and she kept screaming 'Angela' over and over again.","r":true,"m":["scream v. 尖叫；高声喊，大声叫；n. 尖叫声","over and over again adv.一再地；反复不断地"]},{"id":"e04p0308","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"So what do you think the significance of the name 'Angela' is?","r":true,"m":["插入语 do you think：疑问词仍然放最前，后面的从句恢复陈述语序","significance n. 重要性，意义；意思，含义"]},{"id":"e04p0309","s":"Alice","t":"Actually, that's my real name.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0310","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Her real name? That doesn't make any sense, I've seen her driver's license, it did not say 'Angela'.","r":true,"m":["it doesn't make any sense 这完全说不通 / 这毫无道理 / 我完全搞不懂","driver's license 驾驶执照","It did not say 'Angela'. 它（根据上下文判断）没有提到安吉拉。英语里牌子、文件、信件、表格用 say 表示上面写着。"]},{"id":"e04p0311","s":"Susan","t":"Bree, what does it say on the rest of the tape?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0312","s":"Bree","t":"Just more about her nightmares, and this girl she was afraid of.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0313","s":"Gabrielle","t":"So what the hell do we do now?","r":true,"m":["what do we do? 我们该怎么办？/ 我们要做什么？What do you do? 你是做什么工作的？"]},{"id":"e04p0314","s":"Susan","t":"I think we should show Paul the note.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0315","s":"Lynette","t":"Are you sure? He's gonna freak.","r":true,"m":["日常更多的还是用 freak out 搭配，表示崩溃、抓狂、吓疯了"]},{"id":"e04p0316","s":"Bree","t":"Well, it's now or never, I mean I saw what he's asking for the place, it's gonna sell quickly.","r":true,"m":["it's now or never 机不可失，时不再来","the place = 这套房子 ask for + 价格 表示开价、要价"]},{"id":"e04p0317","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Can I say something? I'm glad Paul is moving. I'm sorry, he's just always given me the creeps.","r":true,"m":["give sb the creeps 使某人毛骨悚然；浑身不自在 creep v. 爬行，匍匐"]},{"id":"e04p0318","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Haven't you guys noticed he has this dark thing going on. Is there something about him that just feels...","r":true,"m":["has...going on 表示有…… 正在发生或者身上内心有种说不清的特质、状态 He has this dark thing going on.他身上有股阴郁的劲儿在涌动。"]},{"id":"e04p0319","s":"Lynette","t":"Malignant?","r":true,"m":["malignant adj. 恶性的，致命的；恶毒的，恶意的"]},{"id":"e04p0320","s":"Susan","t":"We've all sort of felt it.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0321","s":"Bree","t":"That being said, I do love what he's done with that lawn.","r":true,"m":["That being said 话虽如此，尽管如此"]}]},{"id":"p04","title":"Julie 鼓励 Susan 追求 Mike","lines":[{"id":"e04p0401","s":"Julie","t":"Mom, the dish is clean. I still don't understand why you don't just ask him out on an 'official date' date.","r":true,"m":["dish n. 器皿总称（盘、碗、碟都算 dish）plate 是 dish 的一种，扁平的那个盘子 Do the dishes.固定搭配：洗碗。","official adj. 正式的，官方的，官方授权的；公务的，公职的；","on a date 约会"]},{"id":"e04p0402","s":"Susan","t":"I'm trying a new strategy, I'm playing hard to get.","r":true,"m":["try doing 试着做某事 try to do 努力去做某事","strategy n. 策略，行动计划；战略，战略学","play hard to get 装作难以追求；欲擒故纵"]},{"id":"e04p0403","s":"Julie","t":"How long do you think you can keep that up?","r":true,"m":["keep it up 继续保持；坚持下去"]},{"id":"e04p0404","s":"Susan","t":"Maybe until noon. Then I'm going to have to run over there and beg him to love me.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0405","s":"Julie","t":"Mom, I don't think you're gonna be able to wait that long.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0406","s":"Susan","t":"You gotta be kidding, she washed her car yesterday. Oh no, she's not. Yep, she's bringing out the big guns.","r":true,"m":["bring out the big guns 放大招；使出浑身解数；动用重要力量 gun n.枪，炮"]},{"id":"e04p0407","s":"Julie","t":"You'd better get over there, she's wearing cotton.","r":true,"m":["get over there 到那边去 run over there","cotton n. 棉，棉花；棉布；棉线，棉纱；wear cotton 穿棉质衣物"]},{"id":"e04p0408","s":"Susan","t":"What am I supposed to say to Mike? I saw you half-naked and I thought I'd drop by? What's that?","r":true,"m":["be supposed to = 应该/该怎么","I thought I'd... = I thought I would...我原打算 / 我当时会……","drop by 顺便拜访"]},{"id":"e04p0409","s":"Julie","t":"A piece of Mike's junk mail we got by mistake, I held on to it in case of an emergency.","r":true,"m":["mail 邮件，是不可数名词 junk mail 垃圾邮件","a piece of 一片/一封/一件 + 不可数名词，piece就是给不可数名词的量词单位，如 a piece of paper","hold on v. 保留，继续持有（常与 to 连用）；紧握，抓住（常与 to 连用）；等待，稍候（电话）；坚持，挺住","in case of 万一；如果发生；假设","emergency n.突发事件，紧急情况；急诊病人 adj.紧急情况下的；应急的"]},{"id":"e04p0410","s":"Susan","t":"God bless you.","r":true,"m":["god bless you 上帝保佑你 bless v. 求上帝保佑，祈神赐福，祝福；祝圣"]}]},{"id":"p05","title":"Susan 借邮件搭话 Mike","lines":[{"id":"e04p0501","s":"Susan","t":"We got this by mistake. I hope it's not important.","r":true,"m":["by mistake 错误地、无意中、不小心"]},{"id":"e04p0502","s":"Mike","t":"No, it's just a promotion from the Rialto, they're having a film festival.","r":true,"m":["promotion n. 促销，推销；提拔，晋升；促进，提倡；promote","the Rialto 影院的名字:里亚尔托影院","film festival 电影节"]},{"id":"e04p0503","s":"Susan","t":"Well, I guess I've done my good deed for the day. I'll just head back home. Bye.","r":true,"m":["good deed 善行 deed n.行为，行动；契约，证书；功绩，英勇事迹","for the day 一整天，截止到今天","head back home 返回家中 head back 返回"]},{"id":"e04p0504","s":"Mike","t":"Hey, do you like old movies?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0505","s":"Susan","t":"I love old movies.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0506","s":"Eddie","t":"I hate Susan Mayer. Every time I see those big doe eyes of hers, I swear to god I just want to go out and shoot a deer.","r":true,"m":["doe eyes 形容女生温柔大眼固定短语 doe n. 母鹿","of hers 双重所有格，限定词 + 名词 + of + mine/yours/his/hers/ours/theirs/sb’s","a friend of hers == one of her friends 这里 hers 就是 her friends，但不能使用 a friend of her friends","of her 通常后面需要跟一个名词如the story of her life","swear to god 对天发誓；向上帝发誓 swear v. 咒骂，诅咒；发誓；保证","deer n. 鹿 buck：公鹿 doe：母鹿 fawn：小鹿"]},{"id":"e04p0507","s":"Huber","t":"What has she done this time?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0508","s":"Eddie","t":"She is out there throwing herself at Mike Delfino, again.","r":true,"m":["throw yourself at sb. 扑向某人、主动投怀送抱"]},{"id":"e04p0509","s":"Huber","t":"Susan likes Mike?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0510","s":"Eddie","t":"Where the hell have you been, Martha? She has been lusting after him ever since he moved in.","r":true,"m":["lust after sb 痴迷、贪恋某人  lust after sth 贪求、觊觎、极度想要某物，带贬义 lust n. 强烈欲望；","ever since 从那时起一直。但只有 ever since 有副词用法，能独立放在句尾；since 不能单独放在句尾，它后面必须带上名词或者从句。"]}]},{"id":"p06","title":"Lynette 强制双胞胎分班","lines":[{"id":"e04p0601","s":"Lynette","t":"I got your message, what's going on?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0602","s":"Teacher","t":"The boys refuse to be separated.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0603","s":"Lynette","t":"They refuse? They're six years old, make them.","r":true,"m":["make them 在这个语境中意思是 “强迫他们（做某事）”"]},{"id":"e04p0604","s":"Teacher","t":"The school regulations are pretty strict about me wrestling with the boys.","r":true,"m":["regulation n. 规章制度，规则；管理，控制","be strict about sth 对某事要求严格、明令限制 strict adj. 要求严格的，严厉的；","wrestle with 与…摔跤，扭打；全力对付，努力克服；苦思 wrestle v. 摔跤，扭打；使劲搬动；努力解决"]},{"id":"e04p0605","s":"Teacher","t":"But if you want to give it a shot, be my guest.","r":true,"m":["give it a shot 尝试一下：尝试做某事 = have a try","be my guest 请便，别客气：用于口语中，表示欢迎对方做某事或拿取某物。"]},{"id":"e04p0606","s":"Lynette","t":"Fine. Which one goes and which one stays?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0607","s":"Teacher","t":"You pick.","r":true}]},{"id":"p07","title":"Gabrielle 和 John 被维修工打断","lines":[{"id":"e04p0701","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I love taking baths, especially with you. It's like taking a vacation from the world.","r":true,"m":["take a bath 洗澡 bath n. 浴缸；洗澡；浴室v. 洗澡，沐浴","especially adv. 尤其，特别；专门，特地；在很大程度上，非常","take a vacation from sth 固定搭配：从…中抽身休假，暂时脱离…","vacation n. 休假，度假 ≈ holiday vocation n.使命感；工作，职业"]},{"id":"e04p0702","s":"John","t":"I hated taking baths when I was a kid. Of course, back then, the only thing I had to play with was my rubber ducky. Who's that? It's Mr. Solis.","r":true,"m":["back then 当时，那会儿","rubber duck 橡皮鸭 ducky 小鸭鸭 rubber n. 橡胶，合成橡胶"]},{"id":"e04p0703","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Relax, Carlos is at work and he doesn't ring the doorbell. It's the cable guy, he's three hours late, use the side entrance.","r":true,"m":["be at work 在上班、在单位、正在工作","ring the doorbell 按门铃","cable guy 有线电视安装维修工 cable n. 电缆；有线电视","side entrance 侧门"]},{"id":"e04p0704","s":"Alice","t":"Gabrielle knew her vacation from the world had ended. What she didn't know was John had left behind a souvenir.","r":true,"m":["souvenir n. 纪念品，纪念物"]}]},{"id":"p08","title":"Bree 做大餐隐瞒 Rex 离家","lines":[{"id":"e04p0801","s":"Danielle","t":"I'm telling you Dad didn't come home last night. They had a fight, a bad one.","r":true,"m":["I'm telling you 我告诉你：表示强调，用于向对方强调某个观点或事实。","mom/dad 前面无 my/your，当作称呼用大写 Dad，前面有物主代词，用小写","have a fight 吵架：指两个或多个人之间的口角或身体冲突"]},{"id":"e04p0802","s":"Andrew","t":"How bad?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0803","s":"Danielle","t":"Like divorce court bad. Listen to her, she always overcompensates when she's worried.","r":true,"m":["divorce court 离婚法庭 court n. 法院，法庭；球场；王宫，宫廷；","like ... bad 聊矛盾、糟糕状况 常见 Like world war three bad 糟糕的像第三次世界大战 Like bad bad. 糟透了","overcompensate vi. 过度补偿 compensate v. 赔偿，偿付；弥补，补偿；抵消；"]},{"id":"e04p0804","s":"Andrew","t":"If dad moves out and leaves us with her, I'll lose my mind.","r":true,"m":["lose my mind 发疯、情绪崩溃、失去理智"]},{"id":"e04p0805","s":"Bree","t":"Dinner is on the table.","r":true,"m":["Dinner is on the table. 家常 Dinner is served. 正式，管家式 Dinner's ready! 最常用"]},{"id":"e04p0806","s":"Andrew","t":"Mom, where did dad go last night?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0807","s":"Bree","t":"He got a last minute call to speak at a medical conference in Philadelphia. Take your seats.","r":true,"m":["a last minute call 临时通知：在最后一刻通知某人某事。","speak at 在某个场合发表演讲或讲话","Philadelphia n. 费城","Take your seats 就座"]},{"id":"e04p0808","s":"Danielle","t":"This marriage is so over.","r":true}]},{"id":"p09","title":"Gabrielle 请的维修工突发意外","lines":[{"id":"e04p0901","s":"Cable guy","t":"Again sorry I was late, the scheduler overbooked me.","r":true,"m":["scheduler n. 计划员；时间调度员；程序机，调度机；","overbook vt. 使过量预订；超额订出"]},{"id":"e04p0902","s":"Gabrielle","t":"How long are you going to be?","r":true,"m":["How long are you going to be (ready)? 你还要多久（才能弄好）？更常用表达：How much longer?"]},{"id":"e04p0903","s":"Cable guy","t":"Almost done, what is that scent? Is that sage and citrus? It's amazing.","r":true,"m":["almost done 快完成了：表示某件事情即将完成或已经接近完成。","scent n. 香味，芳香；气味","sage n. 鼠尾草；智者，圣贤；浅灰绿色 adj. 睿智的，贤明的","citrus n. 柑橘属果树；柑橘类的植物"]},{"id":"e04p0904","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Try to hurry, I have stuff to do.","r":true,"m":["Try to hurry 尽快赶快：尽力加快速度，争取尽快完成某事。"]},{"id":"e04p0905","s":"Carlos","t":"What's happening?","r":true},{"id":"e04p0906","s":"Gabrielle","t":"The cable guy fell, he hit his head on the tub, he may have a concussion.","r":true,"m":["hit v. 打，击；撞击，碰撞；击中","tub n. 盆，桶；","concussion n. 冲击；震荡；脑震荡"]},{"id":"e04p0907","s":"Carlos","t":"It's almost eight.","r":true},{"id":"e04p0908","s":"Gabrielle","t":"He was late.","r":true}]},{"id":"p10","title":"Huber 带肉馅派来要挟 Susan","lines":[{"id":"e04p1001","s":"Huber","t":"Hello, Susan, I made you a pie.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1002","s":"Susan","t":"Wow, why?","r":false},{"id":"e04p1003","s":"Huber","t":"Do I need a motive to do something nice? I can't wait for you to try this, it's mincemeat.","r":true,"m":["motive n. 动机，目的，原因；","can't wait for sb to do sth 迫不及待地等某人做某事","mincemeat 碎肉甜馅，一种用切碎的干果、苹果、糖、香料加上板油熬成的甜馅，最经典的用途是做 mincemeat pie（百果馅饼）英国圣诞节的传统食物。","mince meat 切碎的肉 mince v. 切碎，绞碎；meat n. 肉类，食用肉"]},{"id":"e04p1004","s":"Susan","t":"Actually, I just had dinner.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1005","s":"Huber","t":"That's OK, you can save it for later.","r":true,"m":["save it for later 把它留到以后再用"]},{"id":"e04p1006","s":"Susan","t":"What's so funny?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1007","s":"Huber","t":"I was just thinking of that expression, \"I'll make mincemeat out of you\".","r":true,"m":["expression n. 表达，表示；表情，神情；词语，措词；","I'll make mincemeat out of you 习语，字面意思是我会把你剁成肉酱，实际表达的是我会彻底打败你，我会把你打得落花流水"]},{"id":"e04p1008","s":"Huber","t":"Mincemeat used to be an entree made up of mostly chopped meat, so it was like saying, \"I'll chop you up into little bits\". But that was centuries ago.","r":true,"m":["entree n. （餐厅里或正式宴会上的）主菜；入场许可，加入权","be made up of 构成；由……组成","chopped meat 剁碎的肉 chop v. 剁，砍，劈；","It was like saying... 那就等于说…","chop + up 这里 up 作补语表示彻底做完（相似用法：eat up、use up)","bit n. 小片，小块；小部分，片段 little bits 小碎片；小块","centuries ago 几个世纪前 century n. 世纪；一百年；"]},{"id":"e04p1009","s":"Huber","t":"Today, mincemeat is mostly made up of fruit, spices and rum, there's no meat in it and still people say, \"I'll make mincemeat out of you\".","r":true,"m":["fruit 作水果的总称时是不可数的集合名词，具体表示某个水果时是可数名词","spice n. 香味料，调味料 spicy adj. 加有香料的，辛辣的；刺激的","rum 朗姆酒 champagne 香槟酒 liquor 烈性酒 Margarita 玛格丽塔（一种鸡尾酒名）"]},{"id":"e04p1010","s":"Susan","t":"I don't know that people really say that anymore.","r":true,"m":["I don't know that.. 委婉表达我认为未必 / 不见得，和 I don’t think 逻辑类似，但语气更弱、更不确定"]},{"id":"e04p1011","s":"Huber","t":"I do. So, Susan, how are you?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1012","s":"Susan","t":"I'm fine.","r":false},{"id":"e04p1013","s":"Huber","t":"Good, you know, I have a confession to make. I've always wished I'd been more supportive when Carl left you.","r":true,"m":["confession n. 供认，供状；承认，坦白；忏悔，告解；声明，告白","I have a confession to make. 我有件事要坦白","supportive adj. 支持的，拥护的，给予帮助的"]},{"id":"e04p1014","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, you don't have to apologize about Carl, really, Carl and I are over, I've moved on.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1015","s":"Huber","t":"Yes, I know. You've moved on to that nice Mike Delfino. He is quite a catch, isn't he? You like him, don't you?","r":true,"m":["move on to sb 接触新恋情对象; 继续谈论或处理另一个人","He is quite a catch 他是个很不错的人（尤指作为结婚对象或恋爱对象来说）","quite + a + 名词 表真不愧是…、相当…的 反义：not much of a"]},{"id":"e04p1016","s":"Susan","t":"Sure, as a friend.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1017","s":"Huber","t":"Oh, Susan, being coy is a strategy best employed by virgins at their first dance. For women of our age, it's just annoying. Are you sure you don't want pie?","r":true,"m":["being coy 故作娇羞、忸怩作态 coy adj. 腼腆的；忸怩作态的；怕羞的","employ v. 雇用；使用，利用；忙于，从事","virgin n. 处女，童男；无经验的人，新手；","of our age 和我们年龄相仿"]},{"id":"e04p1018","s":"Susan","t":"No, thank you.","r":false},{"id":"e04p1019","s":"Huber","t":"I hope it works out with you and Mike, you've been so desperate to land him.","r":true,"m":["work out 进展顺利；成功；解决（问题等）work 行不行得通 work out 最终成不成","it works out with sb 和某人之间的事情进展顺利；和某人的关系发展良好","land sb 成功吸引sb；与sb确立恋爱关系/使sb得到（工作、机会等）；为sb谋得（某职位等） land v. 着陆，降落；登陆，上岸； n. 陆地，地面；土地"]},{"id":"e04p1020","s":"Susan","t":"I'm not desperate.","r":false},{"id":"e04p1021","s":"Huber","t":"Good lord, Susan, you burned your rival's house down, if that isn't desperate, I don't know what is.","r":true,"m":["Good lord 天哪：表示惊讶或不满的感叹词。lord n. 主，上帝","rival n. 竞争对手，敌手；","burn the house down == burn down the house 烧毁房屋","当动词短语是动词 + 副词结构，并且宾语是名词（如house）时，副词既可以放在宾语之前，也可以放在宾语之后。如果宾语是代词，副词就只能放在代词之后。例如burn it down（不能说burn down it）"]},{"id":"e04p1022","s":"Susan","t":"Mrs. Huber, with all due respect, you're crazy. What's that?","r":true,"m":["with all due respect 怀着应有的尊重；恕我直言","due adj. 到期的，预期的；应有的，应得的"]},{"id":"e04p1023","s":"Huber","t":"I think you recognize it. I found it in the ruins of Eddie's home.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1024","s":"Susan","t":"Well, that's not ...","r":false},{"id":"e04p1025","s":"Huber","t":"My point is this, I wasn't there for you when Carl left, but I'm here for you now.","r":true,"m":["my point is 我说的是：用于强调自己的观点或要点。"]},{"id":"e04p1026","s":"Huber","t":"As far as I'm concerned, this is our secret, and no one ever need know.","r":true,"m":["as far as I'm concerned 就我而言；在我看来 as far as就……而言","no one needs to know 首选 no one need know 多用于英式书面 / 文艺口语，偏老式"]},{"id":"e04p1027","s":"Huber","t":"Oh, Susan, you don't know how good it feels to finally be able to help you.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1028","s":"Huber","t":"You look so pale, now, I insist you try some of my pie. Go on. Did I mention it's mincemeat?","r":true,"m":["pale adj. （脸色）苍白的；（颜色）浅的，淡的","insist + that 从句 insist v. 坚决要求，执意坚持；坚称"]}]},{"id":"p11","title":"Bree 和 Andrew 爆发争吵","lines":[{"id":"e04p1101","s":"Bree","t":"Open the door, please.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1102","s":"Andrew","t":"Hang on. What?","r":true,"m":["Hang on = hold on 打电话/当面喊停/让某人稍候，两者完全通用"]},{"id":"e04p1103","s":"Bree","t":"May I come in?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1104","s":"Andrew","t":"No.","r":false},{"id":"e04p1105","s":"Bree","t":"I want to talk to you.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1106","s":"Andrew","t":"Then talk.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1107","s":"Bree","t":"Where were you last night?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1108","s":"Andrew","t":"Brian's.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1109","s":"Bree","t":"I just spoke to Brian's mother, now tell me again where you were last night and this time don't lie to me.","r":true,"m":["lie v. 撒谎 lied/lied n. 谎言，谎话  tell lies 说谎","lie v. 平躺；位于 lay/lain n. 方向，位置","lay v. 安放，放置；铺放 laid/laid"]},{"id":"e04p1110","s":"Andrew","t":"Where did you say dad was again? In Philadelphia?","r":true,"m":["疑问词 +【do you think /did you say】+ 陈述语序从句 → 插入语结构"]},{"id":"e04p1111","s":"Bree","t":"Andrew, don't change the subject.","r":true,"m":["change the subject 转换话题"]},{"id":"e04p1112","s":"Andrew","t":"I'm sorry, I thought this subject was telling lies. I called Dad's cellphone, I know he moved out.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1113","s":"Bree","t":"Well, it's just temporary and... I thought it would upset you so I was protecting you.","r":true,"m":["temporary adj. 暂时的，临时的；短期的，短暂的"]},{"id":"e04p1114","s":"Andrew","t":"Whatever, you lied, so stop pretending like you have some sort of moral authority.","r":true,"m":["stop pretending (like) + 从句 别装作……样子","moral authority 道德权威 authority n. 专家，权威人士；权威，威信；许可"]},{"id":"e04p1115","s":"Bree","t":"Andrew, just because I chose not to share my marital problems with you does not give you the right to be rude.","r":true,"m":["just because 特殊结构引导从句作主语，表达仅仅因为这件事。Just because I said yes doesn't mean I agree.我答应≠我认同。","choose not to do sth 选择不做...","give you the right to 赋予你……的权利","rude adj. 粗鲁的，无礼的；粗俗的，下流的"]},{"id":"e04p1116","s":"Andrew","t":"How about driving my father away? Do I get to be rude then?","r":true,"m":["drive sb away 赶走某人","get to do sth. 被允许做某事；有机会/有资格做某事；开始做某事"]}]},{"id":"p12","title":"Carlos 发现陌生男士袜子","lines":[{"id":"e04p1201","s":"Carlos","t":"What's this?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1202","s":"Gabrielle","t":"It's a sock.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1203","s":"Carlos","t":"It's a man's sock. I found it under our bed. It's not mine.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1204","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Oh, for god's sake, Carlos, it's Yao Lin's.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1205","s":"Carlos","t":"Our maid wears size 13 gym socks?","r":true,"m":["maid n. 女仆，女佣；","gym socks 运动袜"]},{"id":"e04p1206","s":"Gabrielle","t":"No, she dusts with them. See? Socks instead of rags.","r":true,"m":["dust v. 擦去…的灰尘；把粉末撒于 n. 灰尘；粉末；尘雾；除尘，掸灰；","instead of 介词短语：代替，而不是；后面接名词、代词或动名词(doing)，用来引出被舍弃的选项。","rag n. 抹布，破布；"]}]},{"id":"p13","title":"Huber 在超市要挟 Susan 替她付费","lines":[{"id":"e04p1301","s":"Huber","t":"Susan, hello, did you and Mike come together? I saw him over in the fresh produce aisle.","r":true,"m":["fresh produce 新鲜农产品 produce 农产品；成果，结果","fresh produce aisle 超市的新鲜农产品通道 Snack Aisle 零食通道","aisle 座位/货架之间的过道（飞机、教堂、影院、超市）corridor 公共建筑里的长走廊（办公楼、酒店、医院、学校） hallway 住宅内部连接各房间的通道"]},{"id":"e04p1302","s":"Susan","t":"No, like I told you before, we’re just friends.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1303","s":"Susan","t":"By the way, if I didn’t make it clear yesterday, I absolutely did not do that thing you accuse me of.","r":true,"m":["accuse sb of sth 指责某人…；控告某人… accuse v. 控告，指控；指责"]},{"id":"e04p1304","s":"Huber","t":"Nice to see you, Mike.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1305","s":"Mike","t":"Hey, you like Alfred Hitchcock? They’re doing a retrospective down at the Rialto.","r":true,"m":["Alfred Hitchcock 阿尔弗雷德·希区柯克 英国导演","retrospective n. （艺术家作品）回顾展 adj. 回顾的，回想的；","up at /down at + 地点 表示在某个地方，带有方向感"]},{"id":"e04p1306","s":"Susan","t":"Uh, I’m not really a fan.","r":true,"m":["I'm not a fan 表示对某事物或某人不感兴趣或不喜欢。fans 粉丝的来源"]},{"id":"e04p1307","s":"Mike","t":"Come on, how can you not like Hitchcock?","r":true,"m":["how can you 你怎么能：指责或质问某人为什么做了某事，表示不理解或不满意。"]},{"id":"e04p1308","s":"Susan","t":"I just, uh, don’t.","r":false},{"id":"e04p1309","s":"Mike","t":"Oh, OK. Well, nice to see you. You too, Mrs. Huber.","r":false},{"id":"e04p1310","s":"Huber","t":"You’re so silly, pretending not to like him on my account. I mean, really.","r":true,"m":["silly adj. 愚蠢的，傻的；嬉笑滑稽的；失去理智的；微不足道的，不实用的；","pretend to do（肯定）/ pretend not to do（否定）/ pretend (that) 从句（标准）/ pretend like 从句（口语，正式换 as if）","on my account 因为我、因为某人的缘故、为了某人"]},{"id":"e04p1311","s":"Susan","t":"Will you just drop it?","r":true,"m":["Will you just drop it? 你能不能别再提这事了？；你能不能就此打住啊？drop it 这里表示别再提了；Will you...? 比 Could/Would 少了一层虚拟语气的缓冲，偏强硬"]},{"id":"e04p1312","s":"Huber","t":"You shouldn’t be rude to me, Susan. Your secret is not an easy burden to bear.","r":true,"m":["burden n.负担，责任 bear v.承受，容忍 bear a burden 承受负担；承担责任"]},{"id":"e04p1313","s":"Huber","t":"That insurance company is putting Eddie through hell. But still, I’ve said nothing.","r":true,"m":["insurance company 保险公司 insurance n. 保险；保险费；保险业；","put sb through hell 让某人经历极度痛苦（或磨难、煎熬）","but still 尽管如此；即便这样；然而"]},{"id":"e04p1314","s":"Huber","t":"The longer it takes for her to get payment, the longer she’ll be staying with me, eating me out of house and home, using up my hot water.","r":true,"m":["the + 比较级..., the + 比较级... 表达一个变化引起另一个变化；越……，就越……","It takes sb + 时间 + to do sth == It takes + 时间 + for sb to do sth 某人做某事花费（多长时间）","payment n. 支付款项，支付额；付款，支付；报答，报复","will be staying 而不是 will stay 表示将会处于住着的状态","eat sb. out of house and home 莎士比亚原句习语：把我吃到倾家荡产","use up 用尽， up = 彻底完成"]},{"id":"e04p1315","s":"Susan","t":"What exactly is it you want from me, Mrs. Huber?","r":true,"m":["exactly adv. 精确地，确切地；（用于强调）恰好，完全；究竟，到底"]},{"id":"e04p1316","s":"Cashier","t":"Are these together?","r":true,"m":["Cashier 收银员，出纳员"]},{"id":"e04p1317","s":"Susan","t":"Ring it up.","r":true,"m":["Ring it up 购物结账的地道说法：把它结一下账 ring up 结账、录入收银机"]}]},{"id":"p14","title":"Lynette 纠结是否给双胞胎用药","lines":[{"id":"e04p1401","s":"Bree","t":"If the school and the pediatrician both think the twins could stand to be medicated, then what’s the problem?","r":true,"m":["pediatrician n. 儿科医生（paediatrician 的美式拼写）","stand v. 忍受，容忍；经得起，经受；站，站立；起立；保持有效，维持不变【固定搭配】could stand to do sth 不妨……，应该……，做……会更好","medicate v. 用药治疗；加药品于"]},{"id":"e04p1402","s":"Lynette","t":"I used to run a company with 85 people, and now I can’t wrangle three small boys without doping them?","r":true,"m":["run a company 经营一家公司","can’t do A without doing B 不做 B 就做不了 A","wrangle 本义：争吵、争辩；口语里 = 费劲管束、哄住、看管一群闹腾的人/小孩","dope v. 给…服用麻醉剂/兴奋剂/止痛药/安眠药；== drug sb"]},{"id":"e04p1403","s":"Lynette","t":"Talk about feeling like a failure.","r":true,"m":["别提有多挫败了 / 说起来，感觉自己就是个失败者。","Talk about + 名词/动名词 这里不是谈论关于…的意思，而是用来加强感叹。","failure n. 失败，失败者"]},{"id":"e04p1404","s":"Bree","t":"Lynette, you’re a great mother. But, let’s face it, your kids are a challenge.","r":true,"m":["主语是多个人/东西，但把这一整组、整件事看成一个整体的情况，表语就可以用 a + 单数名词。"]},{"id":"e04p1405","s":"Lynette","t":"Thank you. That’s the nicest way you could’ve said that.","r":true,"m":["That’s the nicest way you could’ve said that. 这已经是你能想到的最委婉的说法了。","the + 最高级 + 名词 + (that) sb could have done 某人所能做到的最…… 的……"]},{"id":"e04p1406","s":"Lynette","t":"You know, the truth is, when they’re not making me want to tear my hair out, they’re actually really sweet.","r":true,"m":["tear my hair out 非常生气或焦虑，以至于想要拔掉自己的头发。tear /teə(r)/v. 撕扯、撕裂 tear /tɪə(r)/n. 眼泪"]},{"id":"e04p1407","s":"Lynette","t":"I’m afraid if I change the bad stuff, I’m going to change the good stuff.","r":true,"m":["I’m afraid that 表达担忧、害怕的情绪; I'm sorry that 表达歉意或遗憾","bad stuff 不好的东西 good stuff 好东西"]},{"id":"e04p1408","s":"Bree","t":"It’s a tough call.","r":true,"m":["It’s a tough call. 这是个艰难的决定；这是个棘手的选择"]},{"id":"e04p1409","s":"Lynette","t":"Like this mug, I love this mug. If I medicate them, are they still going to make me a mug like this?","r":true,"m":["mug n. 大杯，马克杯"]},{"id":"e04p1410","s":"Bree","t":"You know it’s leaking.","r":true,"m":["leak v. 渗入，漏出；漏，渗漏；泄露，透露 n. 漏洞，裂缝；"]},{"id":"e04p1411","s":"Lynette","t":"Yeah, I know.","r":false}]},{"id":"p15","title":"主妇们将神秘字条交给 Paul","lines":[{"id":"e04p1501","s":"Susan","t":"We talked to Paul, we told him we need to show him something.","r":true,"m":["show sb sth 向某人展示某物"]},{"id":"e04p1502","s":"Gabrielle","t":"He is on his way over.","r":true,"m":["on one’s way (to …) 在某人去往…的路上 on my way to school 在我上学路上 on one’s way over 正在赶来（到我们这边）on the way 在路上"]},{"id":"e04p1503","s":"Susan","t":"So Paul, we notice that you’re selling the house.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1504","s":"Paul","t":"Yes, too many painful memories, I’m sure you understand.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1505","s":"Susan","t":"Before you move, we thought there’s something you should know.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1506","s":"Lynette","t":"It seems there may be more to Mary Alice’s death than you are aware of.","r":true,"m":["It seems that 似乎…；好像…；看样子…","there may be 可能有；也许有","There is more to sth (than …) 事情另有隐情、不止表面看到的那样 关于某事，远不止…"]},{"id":"e04p1507","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Remember when you asked us to pack her things? Well, when we did, we found a note.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1508","s":"Bree","t":"And we think that you should have it.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1509","s":"Susan","t":"You can see from the postmark, Mary Alice probably got it the day she died. Paul, are you going to be okay?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1510","s":"Paul","t":"No.","r":false}]},{"id":"p16","title":"Gabrielle 就袜子一事叮嘱 John","lines":[{"id":"e04p1601","s":"Carlos","t":"Have you always cleaned with socks?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1602","s":"Yao Lin","t":"Yes.","r":false},{"id":"e04p1603","s":"Carlos","t":"What is that, a Japanese thing?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1604","s":"Yao Lin","t":"I’m Chinese. I don’t like lying.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1605","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, I don’t like your ironing, so there.","r":true,"m":["iron v.熨，烫n.铁；熨斗；铁器 ironing n. 熨烫；熨衣服；","so there. 就这样：用于以有点粗鲁、愤怒或孩子气的方式表达自己已经陈述了自己的观点或决定，并且不会改变它。"]},{"id":"e04p1606","s":"John","t":"Mrs. Solis, what are you doing here?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1607","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Carlos found this under the bed.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1608","s":"John","t":"Oh, crap.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1609","s":"Gabrielle","t":"It’s OK. It was a close call, but I managed to cover.","r":true,"m":["a close call 固定短语:千钧一发、死里逃生、侥幸脱险","manage to do 设法做到 manage to cover 设法覆盖、遮盖"]},{"id":"e04p1610","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I got you these. So from now on, we can’t let Carlos see you around the house wearing anything resembling a gym sock.","r":true,"m":["from now on 从现在开始","这里是 see sb +介词短语 的形式，如果是 you are around，多了 are 就是 see + (that)从句的形式","resemble v. 像，与……相似；比 like 更倾向于外形近似"]},{"id":"e04p1611","s":"John","t":"You want me to mow your lawn in sandals, I could lose a toe.","r":true,"m":["sandal n. 凉鞋；檀香 in sandals穿着凉鞋 slippers 拖鞋","toe n. （人的）脚趾，（兽、鸟的）趾；"]},{"id":"e04p1612","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Imagine what you’d lose if Carlos finds out you’re trimming more than the hedges.","r":true,"m":["Imagine what you would... 想象一下你会……","trim v. 修剪，修整；削减，减少；修饰"]},{"id":"e04p1613","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Why are your friends staring at me? Did you tell them about us?","r":true,"m":[" stare at sb/sth 盯着某人/某物看"]},{"id":"e04p1614","s":"John","t":"No, they’re staring ‘cause they think you’re hot.","r":true}]},{"id":"p17","title":"Andrew 深夜未归且挂了 Bree 的电话","lines":[{"id":"e04p1701","s":"Bree","t":"It’s 9:30. What is your brother thinking?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1702","s":"Danielle","t":"Want my advice? Call dad. go tell him to kick Andrew’s ass.","r":true,"m":["advice n. 忠告，劝告，建议 Want my advice? 想要我的建议吗？ == Would you like my advice?","kick sb’s ass 不正式:揍某人一顿；狠狠教训某人；给某人点颜色看看 == teach sb a lesson / punish sb","kick v. 踢，踢腿"]},{"id":"e04p1703","s":"Bree","t":"I am perfectly capable of handling this without your father. Where’s your cellphone? Call Andrew and find out where he is.","r":true,"m":["perfectly adv. 完美地，极佳地；绝对地，完全地","be capable of doing sth 有能力……，能够……"]},{"id":"e04p1704","s":"Danielle","t":"Mom, he is gonna know you are behind this.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1705","s":"Bree","t":"No, he won’t. Just act normal.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1706","s":"Danielle","t":"Hey, it’s me. What’s going on? He knows.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1707","s":"Bree","t":"Andrew, this is your mother. I am rapidly reaching the end of my patience with you.","r":true,"m":["rapidly adv. 快速地，迅速地","patience n. 耐心；耐性；忍耐力 patient adj. 能忍耐的，有耐心的 n. 病人，患者；","I am rapidly reaching the end of my patience with you. 我对你快要彻底失去耐心了。"]},{"id":"e04p1708","s":"Bree","t":"Where are you? Are you at a bar? Andrew! He hung up on me.","r":true,"m":["hang up on sb（没礼貌地）挂断某人的电话 hang up 挂断电话"]},{"id":"e04p1709","s":"Danielle","t":"What are you gonna do?","r":true}]},{"id":"p18","title":"Bree 到脱衣舞俱乐部找到 Andrew","lines":[{"id":"e04p1801","s":"Bree","t":"Heath, Lan, Andrew.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1802","s":"Andrew","t":"Mom, how did you even know I was here? You went in my room?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1803","s":"Bree","t":"You think that’s bad? Tomorrow morning I’m cleaning it.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1804","s":"Bree","t":"By the way, Heath, I didn’t get a chance to tell you, that was a lovely solo last week at church.","r":true,"m":["solo n.单人表演"]},{"id":"e04p1805","s":"Heath","t":"Thank you, we’re out of here.","r":true,"m":["We’re out of here 咱们走！我们这就撤了。"]},{"id":"e04p1806","s":"Bree","t":"I hope it wasn’t something I said. Well, Andrew, shall we?","r":true,"m":["I hope it wasn’t something I said. 我希望不是我说的什么话（导致了不好的情况）","shall we (leave)? Shall we do sth? 提建议，我们做某事好吗？"]},{"id":"e04p1807","s":"Andrew","t":"You just humiliated me in front of my friends. I’m not going anywhere with you.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1808","s":"Bree","t":"Fine.","r":false},{"id":"e04p1809","s":"Andrew","t":"What are you doing?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1810","s":"Bree","t":"I’m staying for the show. I’m dying to see what all the fuss is about.","r":true,"m":["fuss n. 大惊小怪，紧张不安；","what all the fuss is about 固定句式：到底在闹什么、究竟有什么好大惊小怪的；all修饰the fuss","what the fuss is all about 这场骚动究竟是因何而起；be all about sth 口语：核心是，全部围绕着。两句语法都正确，日常口语大多可互换"]},{"id":"e04p1811","s":"Bree","t":"Excuse me, waitress, I’ll have a glass of your house Chardonnay.","r":true,"m":["Chardonnay n. 夏敦埃酒（白葡萄酒）chardonnay ∈ white wine  wine. house wine：餐厅/酒吧的本店招牌酒、店酒","wine: red wine 红葡萄酒 | white wine (chardonnay) 白葡萄酒 | sparkling wine (champagne) 气泡葡萄酒"]},{"id":"e04p1812","s":"Bree","t":"I’m curious, Andrew. As you fantasize about this woman, do you ever stop and think how she came to be on this runway?","r":true,"m":["fantasize about sb 幻想某人；对某人抱有幻想","runway n. T型台；（机场的）跑道；伸展台"]},{"id":"e04p1813","s":"Bree","t":"That’s someone’s little girl, and that someone probably had a lot of dreams for her, dreams that did not include a thong and a pole.","r":true,"m":["someone’s little girl 某人的小女儿；某人的小女孩","have a lot of dreams for sb 对某人抱有很多期望；为某人怀揣着许多梦想","a thong and a pole. 一条丁字裤和一根杆子。thong n. 皮带；皮鞭；人字拖鞋 pole n. 杆，柱 pole dancing 钢管舞"]},{"id":"e04p1814","s":"Andrew","t":"It’s not gonna work, OK? I’m not budging.","r":true,"m":["It’s not gonna work 这行不通；这不会起作用","I’m not budging. 我不会让步；我寸步不让 budge v.（使）稍微移动；budge侧重难以移动；scoot侧重主动挪身体腾出空间 budget n. 预算"]},{"id":"e04p1815","s":"Bree","t":"God only knows what she’s had to deal with in life. Abject poverty, drugs, domestic violence, maybe even molestation.","r":true,"m":["God only knows 天晓得 / 只有上帝知道……（表示没人清楚，充满感慨）","has had to（现在完成时）：强调从过去到一生当中，经历过，不得不承受","abject poverty 赤贫，一贫如洗 abject adj.adj. 极坏的，糟糕透顶的，悲惨的 poverty n. 贫穷，贫困","molestation n. 骚扰；猥亵；干扰，妨害；折磨；调戏"]},{"id":"e04p1816","s":"Bree","t":"Now she treats herself the way other men treat her. Like an object, a piece of meat.","r":true,"m":["the way (that/in which) 引导方式状语从句the way + 从句 = 以…的方式；that/in which 常省略。"]},{"id":"e04p1817","s":"Man","t":"That does it. Kid, get her out of here. She’s killing it for the rest of us.","r":true,"m":["That does it. 够了；行了；就这样了","get sb out of here 让某人离开这里；把某人弄出这儿","kill it 多用于表示做得超棒、大获成功、表现炸裂 You killed it! 你太厉害了！但这这句话中 kill 取毁掉、扼杀的本义，类似于 kill the mood 破坏气氛。整句话可以理解为：她在这儿把我们剩下所有人的兴致都搞没了。"]}]},{"id":"p19","title":"Susan 像 Julie 坦白被 Huber 留言勒索的事","lines":[{"id":"e04p1901","s":"Phone message","t":"We’re not here, leave a message.","r":true,"m":["Phone message 电话留言：在电话未接通时，留下的语音。"]},{"id":"e04p1902","s":"Huber","t":"It’s Mrs. Huber, Susan, are you there? I can see your lights are on. I hope you’re not screening, That’s so tacky.","r":true,"m":["lights are on 灯亮着 lights are off 灯关了","I hope you’re not screening 我希望你不是在故意不接（电话、应门等）screen 在这有故意回避、躲着不见访客的意思","tacky adj. 俗气的；发黏的；缺乏教养或风度的"]},{"id":"e04p1903","s":"Huber","t":"Listen, I need to talk to you. My water heater just burst, and it’s gonna cost me $600 to get a new one, and I can’t afford that.","r":true,"m":["water heater 热水器","burst v. 爆炸，爆裂，胀开；冲，闯，突然出现 -> burst -> burst"]},{"id":"e04p1904","s":"Huber","t":"I’m just beside myself, call me as soon as you get in.","r":true,"m":["I’m just beside myself 我简直要发狂了；我情绪失控了 beside oneself (with sth) 因…而情绪失控","call me as soon as you get in. 你一到家就马上给我打电话。"]},{"id":"e04p1905","s":"Susan","t":"Julie, honey, wake up. We need to talk.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1906","s":"Julie","t":"Can’t this wait until morning?","r":true,"m":["Can’t this wait... 这事难道不能等等…吗？Can't you wait? 你就不能等一等吗？"]},{"id":"e04p1907","s":"Susan","t":"I think I’m being blackmailed...","r":true,"m":["blackmail v./n. 敲诈，勒索；要挟，胁迫"]},{"id":"e04p1908","s":"Susan","t":"And when I realized I couldn’t put out the fire, I ran. I must’ve dropped the measuring cup in the process.","r":true,"m":["put out the fire 扑灭火焰，停止火灾 put out v. 扑灭，熄灭","in the process 在过程中；在进行中 process n. 步骤，程序"]},{"id":"e04p1909","s":"Julie","t":"Why do I even let you out of the house?","r":true},{"id":"e04p1910","s":"Susan","t":"Obviously, I can’t let her get away with this. The only thing to do is go to the police and tell them what happened.","r":true,"m":["get away with sth 做坏事而不受惩罚、侥幸逃脱（惩罚）","The only thing to do is (to) do sth 唯一要做的事就是……","go to the police 报警"]},{"id":"e04p1911","s":"Julie","t":"You can’t do that.","r":true},{"id":"e04p1912","s":"Susan","t":"Julie, I don’t think they’ll throw me in jail. I mean, it was an accident.","r":true,"m":["throw sb in jail 把某人关进监狱"]},{"id":"e04p1913","s":"Julie","t":"Dad won’t care if it was an accident. You know he’ll just use this as an excuse to reopen custody. Mom, I don’t want to live with Dad.","r":true,"m":["use sth as an excuse to do sth 把某事当作做某事的借口"]},{"id":"e04p1914","s":"Susan","t":"I know.","r":false}]},{"id":"p20","title":"Carlos盘问 John 维修工到访一事","lines":[{"id":"e04p2001","s":"Carlos","t":"I need to talk to you.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2002","s":"John","t":"Cool, sure.","r":false},{"id":"e04p2003","s":"Carlos","t":"You were working Tuesday, right? Do you remember the cable guy showing up? And you usually work till what time, five?","r":true,"m":["Tuesday n. 星期二 Monday Tuesday Wednesday Thursday Friday Saturday Sunday","remember sb doing sth：记得某人做过某事（动作已发生）remember sb doing → 记得有这件事（有没有发生这件事）remember when sb did → 记得这件事发生的时间（何时发生）","show up 露面，上门，到场，到达，出现 / 揭露或披露 / 显露，显示","till 直到…… 为止 == until"]},{"id":"e04p2004","s":"John","t":"Yeah.","r":false},{"id":"e04p2005","s":"Carlos","t":"Damn it. That means he was in the house for four hours.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2006","s":"John","t":"Wait, now that I think about it. I might not have seen him.","r":true,"m":["now that I think about it. 现在我仔细一想 / 经我这么一想","might have done 过去或许做了 might not have done 过去或许没做"]},{"id":"e04p2007","s":"Carlos","t":"Either you saw him or you didn’t, which is it?","r":true,"m":["either A or B 要么 A 要么 B（二选一），谓语就近原则","neither A nor B：A 和 B 两者都不，谓语就近原则 both A and B：A 和 B 两者都，谓语用复数"]},{"id":"e04p2008","s":"John","t":"I didn’t.","r":false},{"id":"e04p2009","s":"Carlos","t":"John, did my wife ask you to lie for her?","r":true,"m":["lie for sb 为某人说谎；替某人撒谎"]},{"id":"e04p2010","s":"John","t":"Mr. Solis, I really don’t want to get in the middle of anything.","r":true,"m":["get in the middle of sth 卷入某事，掺和进矛盾当中；不想站队、不想掺和别人的纠纷"]},{"id":"e04p2011","s":"Carlos","t":"Thank you, that’s all I needed to know.","r":true,"m":["That’s all I needed to know. 这就是我需要知道的全部内容了（潜台词：我已经得到我想要的答案）"]}]},{"id":"p21","title":"Susan 和 Julie 准备偷回量杯","lines":[{"id":"e04p2101","s":"Susan","t":"OK, let’s run through it one more time.","r":true,"m":["run through 排练；练习/ 快速浏览 /穿过；贯穿/耗尽；花光","one more time 再一次"]},{"id":"e04p2102","s":"Julie","t":"Mom, it’s not brain surgery. You’ll stand guard while I crawl through Mrs. Huber’s doggie door. Once inside, I’ll find the measuring cup. Simple.","r":true,"m":["stand guard 站岗、放风、警戒 guard n. 卫兵，警卫；看守，保卫，警戒；","crawl v. 爬行，匍匐前进；缓慢移动","doggie door 宠物小门（给猫狗进出的小门）doggie = dog（口语昵称）","Once inside = Once (I am) inside 一旦进到里面"]},{"id":"e04p2103","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, god, I hate that I’m turning you into a little thief.","r":true,"m":["turn sb into 把某人变成……；使某人成为……","thief n. 贼，小偷，偷窃犯"]},{"id":"e04p2104","s":"Julie","t":"It’s our measuring cup. We’re just taking back what’s ours.","r":true,"m":["take back 取回；拿回；收回"]},{"id":"e04p2105","s":"Susan","t":"Hey, that’s right. Ethically, we have nothing to be ashamed about. Oh, wear these, I don’t want you to leave fingerprint.","r":true,"m":["Ethically adv. 合乎伦理地；伦理上；环保地","ashamed adj.（人）感到羞愧的，惭愧的。搭配：be ashamed of/about sth 为某事感到羞愧；be ashamed to do sth 羞于做某事","shame n.羞愧，耻辱；憾事；It’s a shame. 真可惜 / v.使蒙羞，使羞愧","fingerprint n. 指纹，手印"]},{"id":"e04p2106","s":"Susan","t":"There she goes, okay, move.","r":true,"m":["There she goes 她走了；她去那边了"]},{"id":"e04p2107","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, so glad to be playing Frisbee again. Here you go, coming atcha.","r":true,"m":["(I’m) so glad to be playing… 很高兴能够做某事（be + doing 强调正在进行的状态）","Frisbee n. （投掷游戏用的）飞盘","coming atcha == coming at you；come at sb：朝某人冲过来、飞向某人"]},{"id":"e04p2108","s":"Susan","t":"All right, back up a little more, there you go.","r":true,"m":["back up a little more 再往后退一点 back up 向后退、往后挪","there you go 好了；就是这样"]},{"id":"e04p2109","s":"Susan","t":"Wow, all right, here we go.","r":true,"m":["here we go == let's go 开始做某事: 咱们开始吧"]},{"id":"e04p2110","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, my, whoops! You'd better go get that.","r":true,"m":["Whoops 哎呀"]}]},{"id":"p22","title":"Mike 邀约 Susan 观看影展","lines":[{"id":"e04p2201","s":"Mike","t":"Hey, Susan, I thought that was you.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2202","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, Julie and I are just out tossing a Frisbee around, and it flew off into Mrs. Huber’s backyard.","r":true,"m":["toss v.（轻轻地或随意地）扔，抛，掷 toss sth to sb = toss sb sth 把某物抛给某人","toss a Frisbee around 来回抛飞盘，around 表示来回、反复","fly off 飞离、飞出去，飞脱 fly -> flew -> flown"]},{"id":"e04p2203","s":"Mike","t":"Oh, you need some help?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2204","s":"Susan","t":"No, Julie’s got it.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2205","s":"Mike","t":"OK, actually, I’m glad I ran into you. I wanted to make sure things were OK between us. The other day, you seemed kind of distant.","r":true,"m":["run into sb 偶然遇见；碰到（某人）/ 撞上；与…… 相撞","things are OK between us 我们两人之间关系还好（美剧描述人际关系高频表达）","the other day 前几天；不久前的某天","kind of = kinda（口语）有点儿，稍微（修饰形容词）= sort of","distant（人）冷淡的、疏远的；（距离）遥远的"]},{"id":"e04p2206","s":"Susan","t":"Distant? What do you mean?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2207","s":"Mike","t":"I mean, you’re not mad at me for some reason, are you?","r":true,"m":["be mad at sb 生某人的气，对某人恼火","for some reason 不知什么原因，莫名其妙"]},{"id":"e04p2208","s":"Susan","t":"No, not at all.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2209","s":"Mike","t":"Good, ‘cause I’m gonna take one more shot at this. I got tickets for a Billy Wilder retrospective, Wednesday night, I’d love to take you with me.","r":true,"m":["have/take a shot at sth 试着做某事、尝试争取；再试一次 give it a shot 尝试一下","Billy Wilder 比利・怀尔德，犹太裔美国导演、编剧和制片人 a Billy Wilder retrospective 名词作定语：比利·怀尔德主题作品回顾展；Billy Wilder's retrospective 名词所有格：比利·怀尔德的回顾展；","take sb with me 带上某人一起"]},{"id":"e04p2210","s":"Susan","t":"You are so sweet. I’d love to go.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2211","s":"Mike","t":"All right.","r":false}]},{"id":"p23","title":"Susan 将 Mike 的电影票让给 Eddie","lines":[{"id":"e04p2301","s":"Susan","t":"Eddie, I thought you’d be at work.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2302","s":"Eddie","t":"I’m not feeling well. I got a sunburn the other day washing my car.","r":true,"m":["I’m not feeling well 我感觉不舒服","sunburn n/v.晒伤"]},{"id":"e04p2303","s":"Susan","t":"Well, don’t just run off, come and hang out with us.","r":true,"m":["run off 跑开，匆匆离开"]},{"id":"e04p2304","s":"Eddie","t":"Boy, you are one sick ticket.","r":true,"m":["you are one sick ticket 你这人真是个奇葩/你脑子不正常/你可真变态。俚语里 ticket 可以指代某一类人、家伙","现在都说：You’re a sicko."]},{"id":"e04p2305","s":"Susan","t":"What?","r":false},{"id":"e04p2306","s":"Eddie","t":"It’s not bad enough I have to watch you throw yourself at him every day. And now you want to make sure that I see it up close and personal?","r":true,"m":["watch sb do sth 看到某人做某事的整个过程，或者经常看到某人做某事 watch sb doing sth 看到某人正在做某事","throw yourself at sb 主动示好、投怀送抱；向某人献殷勤；急切地讨好某人 / 猛地扑向某人","分开写 every day = 每天（表时间，作状语）；连写 everyday = 日常的（形容词，修饰名词）","up close and personal 美式习语：近距离地、亲身地、当面亲眼看到"]},{"id":"e04p2307","s":"Susan","t":"No, it’s not like that.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2308","s":"Mike","t":"I’ve got to take off, but I’ll call you about Wednesday night, OK?","r":true,"m":["I’ve got to take off 我得走了；我得出发了 take off 突然离开、抽身走人；起飞；脱下","about Wednesday night 关于周三晚上这件事 on Wednesday night 在周三晚上 想表达大约在周三晚上用 around 不会引起歧义"]},{"id":"e04p2309","s":"Susan","t":"Eddie, wait. Mike and I were gonna go see the movies on Wednesday and I just thought it would be fun if you joined us.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2310","s":"Eddie","t":"You want me to come with you?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2311","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah. That’s OK, isn’t it, Mike?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2312","s":"Mike","t":"Well, it’s a limited engagement. But it’s sold out, I’ve only got two tickets.","r":true,"m":["limited engagement 限定演出","be sold out 售罄; 卖光"]},{"id":"e04p2313","s":"Susan","t":"Eddie, wait. You should take my ticket.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2314","s":"Eddie","t":"Really? Is that OK with you, Mike?","r":true,"m":["Is that OK with you 这你觉得可以吗？；你能接受吗？；你同意吗？"]},{"id":"e04p2315","s":"Mike","t":"Uh, yeah, sure.","r":false},{"id":"e04p2316","s":"Eddie","t":"So what time do you want to pick me up?","r":true,"m":["pick sb up（开车）接某人"]}]},{"id":"p24","title":"Carlos 殴打维修工","lines":[{"id":"e04p2401","s":"Cable guy","t":"Hang on.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2402","s":"Carlos","t":"You think you can have sex with anyone you want, huh?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2403","s":"Alice","t":"Carlos couldn’t help but feel proud of himself. After all, he’d just defended his honor, or had he?","r":true,"m":["couldn’t help but do sth 固定句型：忍不住、禁不住做某事 = couldn’t help doing sth","be proud of sb/oneself 为…… 感到自豪 / 得意","defend v. 保卫，防御；捍卫，维护； defend one’s honor 捍卫某人的荣誉；维护某人的名誉","or had he (defended his honor)? 反问结构，或者他真的（做了/是这样）了吗？"]},{"id":"e04p2404","s":"Carlos","t":"Are you gay?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2405","s":"Cable guy","t":"Yes, Is that why you’re doing this?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2406","s":"Carlos","t":"Yeah.","r":false}]},{"id":"p25","title":"Paul 编造恶毒字条是 Alice 写的","lines":[{"id":"e04p2501","s":"Lynette","t":"Will you buy some chocolates?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2502","s":"Paul","t":"Ladies.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2503","s":"Lynette","t":"Hey, Paul, what’s up?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2504","s":"Paul","t":"I wanted to apologize for my outburst yesterday.","r":true,"m":["I wanted to… 1.过去打算道歉 2.口语委婉用法，用过去式wanted，语气更柔和、礼貌","outburst n. （火山、情感等的）爆发；情绪失控发火"]},{"id":"e04p2505","s":"Lynette","t":"Don’t worry about it. We unloaded a lot on you.","r":true,"m":["unload v. （从车、船上）卸，取下；倾诉，发泄；unload sth. on sb. 把（烦恼、压力、一堆麻烦事）倾诉 / 一股脑丢给某人","We unloaded a lot on you. 我们跟你倾诉了太多烦心事 / 给你添了不少心理负担。"]},{"id":"e04p2506","s":"Paul","t":"I suppose you’re wondering why I reacted so violently to that note.","r":true,"m":["suppose v. 推断，料想，猜想；假设，假定，设想","react to 对……作出反应","violently adv. 猛烈地，情绪激动地；凶猛地"]},{"id":"e04p2507","s":"Gabrielle","t":"It did cross our minds.","r":true,"m":["It did cross our minds. 我们确实心里有这样的疑惑"]},{"id":"e04p2508","s":"Paul","t":"Well, the truth is, Mary Alice was not a well person. She was very troubled.","r":true,"m":["a well person 身心状态健康正常的人","troubled adj. 不安的，忧虑的，烦恼的；动乱的，混乱的"]},{"id":"e04p2509","s":"Paul","t":"At first it was harmless. She would leave herself notes, reminders like “pick up the milk” or “Zach has a dentist appointment.”","r":true,"m":["harmless adj. 无害的，无恶意的","leave sb notes 给某人留便条 leave sb sth = leave sth for sb 给某人留下某物","reminder n. 提醒条，提示物 reminders 做 notes 的同位语，解释说明便条是用来提醒的。","pick up + 小件商品 顺路随手购买","dentist appointment 牙医预约"]},{"id":"e04p2510","s":"Paul","t":"But over time the notes became ugly. Hateful messages started showing up. Mary Alice was writing them to me, to Zach, to herself.","r":true,"m":["over time 久而久之；随着时间推移","hateful adj. 充满恨意的，恶毒伤人的"]},{"id":"e04p2511","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Really.","r":false},{"id":"e04p2512","s":"Paul","t":"That’s why I lost it. I was reminded of what Zach and I had been through.","r":true,"m":["That’s why I lost it. 这就是我当时情绪失控发火的原因 lost it 失去理智、大发雷霆","remind sb of sth 使某人想起某事/物","be/go through sth 经历（苦难、波折）"]},{"id":"e04p2513","s":"Lynette","t":"Paul, I’m so sorry.","r":false},{"id":"e04p2514","s":"Gabrielle","t":"We had no idea.","r":true,"m":["We had no idea.我们当时一无所知 / 我们完全不知道。have no idea 固定搭配：不知道，完全没头绪"]},{"id":"e04p2515","s":"Paul","t":"Well, anyway, I’d appreciate it if you kept this to yourselves. For Zach’s sake.","r":true,"m":["I would appreciate it if sb did sth 如果某人做某事，我会感激 I would appreciate sb('s) doing sth 感激某人做某事","keep sth to oneself 将此事保密，不要外传","For one’s sake. 为了某人着想"]},{"id":"e04p2516","s":"Lynette","t":"Of course.","r":false},{"id":"e04p2517","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Wow, I think he’s lying.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2518","s":"Lynette","t":"So do I.","r":true,"m":["So do I 我也是"]}]},{"id":"p26","title":"Lynette 放弃给孩子服药","lines":[{"id":"e04p2601","s":"News","t":"Scavo Promoted to Vice President. What next for whiz kid Lynette Scavo.","r":false,"m":["promote to 晋升为 promote v. 促进，提倡；升职，晋升；促销，推广；","Vice President. 副总 vice adj. 副的；代替的，代理的 president n. 总统，负责人，会长，院长，主席；（公司）董事长","whiz kid 神童","What('s)  next for sb (口语省略)某人接下来会怎样；某人下一步是什么"]},{"id":"e04p2602","s":"Lynette","t":"Boys, could you get in here, please?","r":true,"m":["get in here 进来；到这儿来"]},{"id":"e04p2603","s":"Twins1","t":"He broke my plane.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2604","s":"Twins2","t":"I did not.","r":false},{"id":"e04p2605","s":"Lynette","t":"We’ll talk about that later. Right now I need you to take some medicine.","r":true,"m":["take medicine 服药"]},{"id":"e04p2606","s":"Twins1","t":"Are we sick?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2607","s":"Lynette","t":"Not exactly, this is a kind of special medicine. It’s like a vitamin and you’ll take it every day. OK? Stay right there. Now open up.","r":true,"m":["Not exactly 不完全是，不见得","vitamin n. 维生素，维他命（可数）","open up (your mouth) 张大你的嘴 open your mouth 张开嘴 up有充分、彻底打开的意思"]},{"id":"e04p2608","s":"Twins","t":"Nope.","r":false,"m":["Nope adv. 不是，没有；不"]},{"id":"e04p2609","s":"Alice","t":"In that moment, Lynette made a decision. When it came to dealing with her children, medication was no longer an option.","r":true,"m":["When it came to doing sth 当涉及到做某事；当提到做某事；一谈到做某事"]},{"id":"e04p2610","s":"Alice","t":"Of course, given her continuing level of frustration, Lynette also felt a little “self-medication” couldn’t hurt.","r":true,"m":["given (that) 考虑到；鉴于；鉴于…… 情况","continuing adj. 继续的；持续的；连续的 continuing level of + 抽象名词 表示持续存在的…程度/一直维持着…情绪或状态","frustration n. 懊恼，沮丧；受阻，挫败；","self-medication 自我药疗；自行用药","sth wouldn’t/couldn’t hurt 做某事也无妨；并不会有坏处；不妨… 还可以用 It wouldn’t hurt (to do sth) 句式","鉴于自己一直这么心烦意乱，勒奈特觉得稍微 “自我药疗” 一下也无妨。"]}]},{"id":"p27","title":"Bree 主动向 Andrew 道歉","lines":[{"id":"e04p2701","s":"Bree","t":"So what’s your strategy? Are you just never gonna speak to me again?","r":true,"m":["strategy n. 策略，行动计划；战略，战略学"]},{"id":"e04p2702","s":"Andrew","t":"Something like that.","r":true,"m":["Something like that. 类似这样；差不多吧"]},{"id":"e04p2703","s":"Bree","t":"I suppose I do owe you an apology.","r":true,"m":["I do owe you an apology. 我确实欠你一个道歉"]},{"id":"e04p2704","s":"Andrew","t":"Careful, I wouldn’t want you to strain yourself.","r":true,"m":["Careful. 口语省略句 = Be careful. 小心","I wouldn’t want you to do sth 委婉句型：我不想/我可不希望你做某事","strain v.过度用力；拉伤；使（身体）过度疲劳","字面：小心点，我可不希望你把自己累着/勉强到自己。这里是讽刺、挖苦：悠着点，别太勉强自己了"]},{"id":"e04p2705","s":"Bree","t":"I shouldn’t have lied to you about your father. You and your sister are old enough to handle the truth, and I’m sorry.","r":true,"m":["lie to sb about sth 就某事对某人说谎；在某事上向某人撒谎","handle the truth 坦然接受真相、应对真相"]},{"id":"e04p2706","s":"Andrew","t":"Keep going. I’m mad at you for about 7000 other things.","r":true,"m":["Keep going 继续说；接着往下讲","be mad at sb for sth 因某事生某人的气"]},{"id":"e04p2707","s":"Bree","t":"If you think I’m gonna apologize for taking you out of a strip club, you’re wrong. I consider it one of my finest moments.","r":true,"m":["strip club 脱衣舞夜总会 strip v. 除去，撕掉（外皮或表层）；夺去，剥夺；脱衣服 n. 条，带；脱衣舞；","consider + 宾语 + （to be）宾语补足语：经过思考之后，把这件事看作/认定为…"]},{"id":"e04p2708","s":"Bree","t":"Oh, Andrew. I know you blame me for what’s happening with your father, but it’s not entirely my fault and I need you to understand that.","r":true,"m":["blame sb for sth 因某事责备某人；把某事归咎于某人"]},{"id":"e04p2709","s":"Andrew","t":"I do. I just don’t want him to leave.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2710","s":"Bree","t":"Neither do I.","r":true,"m":["Neither do I 我也不想（他离开）"]},{"id":"e04p2711","s":"Andrew","t":"Mom, when can I have my door back?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2712","s":"Bree","t":"Three months.","r":true}]},{"id":"p28","title":"新闻播报维修工遇袭和 Carlos 画像","lines":[{"id":"e04p2801","s":"Reporter","t":"Royal Oaks was the scene of a hate crime today, when Jonathan Lisco, local gay activist and part-time female impersonator, was brutally attacked in his home.","r":true,"m":["Royal Oaks 皇家橡树庄园/小区 royal adj. 皇家的、王室的 oak n. 橡树，栎树；橡木","scene n. 事发地，现场；事件，场面 live on the scene 现场直播","a hate crime 仇恨犯罪：基于性别、性取向等偏见实施的犯罪 crime n. 罪，罪行；犯罪","when = on which day（在这一天），修饰前面的 today","activist n. 活动积极分子，维权人士","impersonator n. 模仿表演者 female impersonator 男扮女装表演者","brutally adv. 残忍地，粗暴凶狠地","attack v. 袭击，殴打；抨击 n. 袭击，攻击；批评，抨击"]},{"id":"e04p2802","s":"Reporter","t":"Lisco speculated the attack was in response to his efforts to secure same-sex partner insurance coverage from his employer, Cliffside Cable.","r":true,"m":["speculate v. 推测，猜想；投机","in response to... 固定短语：作为对……的回应，用 a response to 也可以，但介词固定用 to","effort n. 努力，艰难的尝试；力气，精力；有组织的活动；努力的结果，成就 efforts to do sth 为...所做的努力","secure v. 争取获得、设法拿到；保障 adj. 安全的 secure sth from sb 从…争取到/拿到某物","same-sex adj. 同性的 same-sex partner 同性伴侣","insurance coverage 保险保障、保险赔付范围 coverage n. 覆盖范围；新闻报道；保险范围；课程内容；防守","employer n. 雇主 employee n. 雇员","Cliffside Cable 公司名：克里夫赛德有线电视公司 cliffside n. 悬崖边；崖面","利斯科推测，这次袭击是因为他努力向雇主克里夫赛德有线电视公司争取同性伴侣保险权益而引发的。"]},{"id":"e04p2803","s":"Reporter","t":"Police are circulating this sketch of the assailant.","r":true,"m":["circulate v. 分发，传阅，对外公布；环流，循环 circular adj. 圆形的，环形的；循环的","sketch n. 素描，速写，草图；粗样，初稿；简述，概述","assailant n. 行凶者，袭击者 adj. 行凶的"]},{"id":"e04p2804","s":"Lisco","t":"The circumstances speak for themselves. I’ve taken a strong stance with my company.","r":true,"m":["circumstance n. 条件，情况，环境；境况，经济状况；详情，原委；命运，境遇","speak for themselves 固定习语：不言自明；本身足以说明问题，不用再多解释","stance n. 立场，态度；站姿 strong stance 强硬立场 take a stance (with sb on sth) 表明立场，持某种态度"]},{"id":"e04p2805","s":"Carlos","t":"Is there something you want to ask me?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2806","s":"Gabrielle","t":"No.","r":false}]},{"id":"p29","title":"Huber 发现 Susan 偷走量杯，二人决裂","lines":[{"id":"e04p2901","s":"Huber","t":"You took it, didn’t you?","r":true},{"id":"e04p2902","s":"Susan","t":"Good evening, Mrs. Huber.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2903","s":"Huber","t":"It’s my own fault for not hiding the cup. Obviously, if you‘re capable of arson, I should have known that you’d be capable of breaking and entering.","r":true,"m":["be capable of sth/doing sth 有能力做；能够做出（坏事）","arson n. 纵火；纵火罪","breaking and entering 法律固定名词短语:非法闯入；强行入室罪 break in 闯入；破门而入"]},{"id":"e04p2904","s":"Susan","t":"I don’t know what you’re talking about, Mrs. Huber.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2905","s":"Huber","t":"I suppose you destroyed it.","r":true,"m":["destroy v. 销毁；破坏"]},{"id":"e04p2906","s":"Susan","t":"Again, I don’t know what you’re talking about. But, yeah, I did.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2907","s":"Huber","t":"I was going to keep your secret, It’s a shame you couldn’t trust me.","r":true,"m":["It’s a shame (that) …  ……真遗憾；……真可惜"]},{"id":"e04p2908","s":"Susan","t":"You are a piece of work, do you know that?","r":true,"m":["a piece of work 形容某人难缠、古怪、令人极度反感"]},{"id":"e04p2909","s":"Huber","t":"Oh, Susan, let’s not be unpleasant. We can go back to the same friendly relationship we’ve always had.","r":true},{"id":"e04p2910","s":"Susan","t":"I will keep my lawn looking nice. And I will make sure that my music isn’t played too loud. And if I get some of your mail, heck, I’ll run it right over. Because that’s what good neighbors do.","r":true,"m":["loud 这里做副词， 多用于音量大小，常和 play, speak, sing, laugh 搭配 loudly 则侧重喧闹刺耳","heck int. 见鬼（缓和语气的感叹词）","run sth over 把东西快速送过去"]},{"id":"e04p2911","s":"Susan","t":"But from now on, when I run into you on the street, and I say, “Good morning, Mrs. Huber” or “How are you, Mrs. Huber?”, just know that inside, I’m quietly but decidedly hating your guts.","r":true,"m":["just know that … （祈使句）你只要知道…… inside 在内心深处，心里头","decidedly adv. 果断地；断然地；毫无疑问 quietly but decidedly 表面不动声色，内心却无比坚定","hate sb’s guts 恨透某人；打心底憎恶某人 love sb’s guts：非常欣赏 / 喜欢某人 gut n. 内脏；胆量"]},{"id":"e04p2912","s":"Huber","t":"Careful, dear. Let’s not say things we’ll live to regret.","r":true,"m":["live to regret 日后追悔莫及；迟早会为今天的话后悔 regret v/n. 懊悔，惋惜"]},{"id":"e04p2913","s":"Susan","t":"Good evening, Mrs. Huber.","r":false}]},{"id":"p30","title":"Paul 雇人调查恐吓字条来源","lines":[{"id":"e04p3001","s":"Susan","t":"He actually said Mary Alice was crazy?","r":true},{"id":"e04p3002","s":"Lynette","t":"Not in so many words, but everything Paul said certainly made it seem like she was schizophrenic.","r":true,"m":["Not in so many words 没有明确直说；没有直白讲出来","make it seem like + 从句：使人看起来好像…、给人的印象仿佛 make + sb/sth + do sth 使…… 做某事","schizophrenic adj. 患有精神分裂症的 n. 精神分裂症患者"]},{"id":"e04p3003","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I think he’s hiding something. I know it.","r":true},{"id":"e04p3004","s":"Bree","t":"But wait. What about the tape? I mean, she did say that her name was Angela.","r":true,"m":["What/How about + 名词：…… 怎么样？/…… 呢？单纯转话题、追问某件事的情况，优先 What about，提建议，征求对方想法，或者抛出选项优先 How about"]},{"id":"e04p3005","s":"Lynette","t":"Mary Alice was not crazy.","r":true},{"id":"e04p3006","s":"Bree","t":"My father was a prosecutor and he always said that the simplest explanation was usually the right one.","r":true,"m":["prosecutor n. 检察官，公诉人；刑事控方律师","explanation n. 解释, 说明 explain"]},{"id":"e04p3007","s":"Susan","t":"But remember what the note said: “I know what you did. It makes me sick. And I’m going to tell.”","r":true},{"id":"e04p3008","s":"Susan","t":"That’s not the kind of thing that someone writes to themselves. That’s a message sent by an enemy.","r":true},{"id":"e04p3009","s":"Man","t":"So exactly what is it you hired me to do?","r":true,"m":["What exactly is it (that) 从句? 这里 exactly 放在疑问词前后都表示确切来说、究竟","hire v. 聘用, 雇佣"]},{"id":"e04p3010","s":"Paul","t":"It’s very simple really. Someone sent that note to my wife, and I need to know who.","r":true},{"id":"e04p3011","s":"Alice","t":"What type of person would send such a note? Was it an enemy? Of course.","r":true,"m":["What type of person 什么样的人 = What kind of person","such 可用于修饰单数/复数/不可数名词，名词前可加形容词修饰也可以不加，不加其他形容词表示“这样/这么…”"]},{"id":"e04p3012","s":"Alice","t":"But what kind? An acquaintance? A stranger? Or how about a neighbor that lives a few feet away?","r":true,"m":["acquaintance n. 泛泛之交，认识但不熟的人；相识","a few feet away 相隔几英尺远，形容距离很近"]}]}]};
